 \item For each $i \le j \le k$ in $[n]$, we have $l_{iijk} = l_{ijjk} = l_{ijkk} = e_L$.
 
 \item For each $i \le j \le k \le p$ in $[n]$, we have $m_{iijkp} = m_{ijjkp} = m_{ijkkp} = m_{ijkpp}= e_m$.
