From Figure~\ref{d:PF_lift_wd}, we can derive two different formulas. One is 
\[
l = {\rm id}_{{\rm id}_{\del(h_3)}} \#_1 \{h_2,h_1\} = \act{\del h_3} \{h_2,h_1\}.
\]
 The other is 
 \[
 l =\{{\rm id}_{\del(h_3)}\#_1 h_2, {\rm id}_{\del(h_3)} \#_1h_1 \} =\{\act{\del h_3}h_2,\act{\del h_3}h_1 \} .
 \]
  By Property~\ref{pfeq} of 2-crossed module, these two formulas are identical.

We can now interpret the two new operators in the 3-crossed module — the left-homannian and right-homannian — as illustrated in the diagrams. The left-homannian is a twisted version of Property~\ref{lpl} of 2-crossed module, and it is represented in Figure~\ref{d:lhmn}.
